From d3e3fe02e1027c7e7e9169ed76a8ba181214677d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Catherine Grabar <catherine.grabar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 23:46:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] M2 steps 5-6: ReplayLog and headless fast-forward
 benchmark
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- systems/sim/replay_log.gd: records (gen_seed, [Action...]) with the
  rolled weather stamped on sleep entries; apply_to() rebuilds world +
  GameState from scratch; JSON save/load
- GameState.reset(): new-game/replay baseline mirroring initializers
- farm facade records every ok action; main seeds each run from randi()
  (documented entropy edge) and starts the session log
- Replay determinism test: a scripted session with deliberate RNG noise
  between actions replays from JSON to a byte-identical end-state snapshot
- tools/benchmark_sim.gd: action-stream fast-forward benchmark.
  Desktop result: ~1,900 sim-days/sec, ~156k actions/sec — ~1.15Mx
  realtime vs a 600s nominal day (M2 gate needs >=100x)

Suites: unit 145/145, integration 20/20.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
